NVIDIA Video Codec SDK headers (nv-codec-headers)
  core/src/decode/nvdec/cu/ transcribes structures and constants from
  dynlink_cuviddec.h, dynlink_nvcuvid.h and dynlink_cuda.h as distributed in
  nv-codec-headers (https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers), which are
  under the MIT License (text above), with the copyright notices of NVIDIA
  Corporation and of Timo Rothenpieler given in those headers.

Intel Video Processing Library (libvpl) headers
  core/src/decode/qsv/mfx.rs and core/src/output/video/host/vpl.rs
  transcribe declarations from api/vpl/mfx*.h of libvpl
  (https://github.com/intel/libvpl), under the MIT License (text above):

    Copyright (C) Intel Corporation

libva headers
  core/src/decode/vaapi/ and core/src/decode/qsv.rs transcribe structures
  and constants from va.h, va_drm.h, va_vpp.h and va_dec_hevc.h of libva
  (https://github.com/intel/libva), under the MIT License (text above):

    Copyright (c) 2007-2009 Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.

Linux user-space API headers
  core/src/decode/v4l2/ transcribes structures and constants from
  linux/videodev2.h, linux/v4l2-controls.h, linux/media.h,
  asm-generic/ioctl.h and drm/drm_fourcc.h of the Linux kernel. These
  headers are offered under GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note (videodev2.h and
  v4l2-controls.h also under BSD-3-Clause, drm_fourcc.h under the MIT
  License); the syscall note keeps a program that uses the kernel's
  interface through them from being a derived work of the kernel. Copyright
  the authors named in those headers.

AMD Advanced Media Framework (AMF) headers
  core/src/decode/amf/ and core/src/output/video/host/amf.rs transcribe
  interface layouts from
  amf/public/include of the AMF SDK 1.5 (https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/AMF),
  under the MIT License (text above), with the copyright notice of
  Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. given in those headers.

